<title>UK: Fountain Forestry shares set debut premium.</title>
<headline>Fountain Forestry shares set debut premium.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Fountain Forestry Plc, a forest management company, were quoted at a premium as they made their debut on the London Stock Exchange's Alternative Investment Market (AIM) on Thursday.</p>
<p>The stock was quoted at 84-1/2p by 1505 GMT, up on the placing price of 75p for the three million share issued by brokerage Charles Stanley.</p>
<p>Fountain raised 2.25 million stg in the placing, giving the company a value of 6.6 million stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 5106</p>
